{
  "_note": "Pinned sampling commits. Even-index sampling over a growing history is epoch-dependent, so the printed digits are only reproducible if the sampled commits are fixed. Full 40-character SHAs; derived once, then used verbatim by every later run.",
  "_verified": "httpie's pins reproduce longitudinal_arch_out.json exactly (16/16 commits, cycle_ratio and module count), which verifies the pinning machinery against an artefact created before the machinery existed. The refactor that replaced in-place `git checkout` with a detached worktree reproduces the same 16/16 httpie readings, so the isolation change costs nothing.",
  "_n_samples": "16 for these architecture curves. longitudinal.py's function-duplication curves use 24. The two are deliberately different: moving these to 24 would change every printed digit, httpie's included, and forfeit the verification above.",
  "_measured_at": "2026-08",
  "_dumps": "experiments/data/longitudinal_arch_<lib>.json is the reading of record. <lib>_no-type-checking.json is the sensitivity variant with `if TYPE_CHECKING:` imports excluded. longitudinal_arch_out.json is the pre-pinning httpie record and is never rewritten.",
  "_regenerate": "tools/evidence-check.sh (re-measures at these SHAs and exits 1 on any numeric difference). Re-deriving pins changes every printed digit at once and needs a written reason.",
